From b1d0a9ed0f4433173d5ab45ea66de1315cd3f984 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 06:46:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 605/638] Implement file dialogs on AROS with the ASL file
 requester

AROS built shell_dialog_stub.cc, whose CreateSelectFileDialog() returns
nullptr. SelectFileDialog::Create() hands that straight back and callers
dereference it, so the browser process died with 0x80000003 illegal
address access in ui::SelectFileDialog::Sele... on anything that opens a
chooser: Downloads "Change", Save As, or an <input type=file> on a page.
A missing platform piece presenting as a crash on ordinary use.

Adds SelectFileDialogAros, backed by asl.library's ASL_FileRequest:

- Open, Save As, multi-select and the three folder types all map onto
  ASLFR_DoSaveMode / ASLFR_DoMultiSelect / ASLFR_DrawersOnly.
- Chromium's extension groups become an ASL pattern, so
  {{"htm","html"},{"txt"}} shows as "(#?.htm|#?.html|#?.txt)".
  include_all_files or a "*" entry means no filter at all.
- The requester is modal and blocks its thread, so it runs on a
  MayBlock()/USER_BLOCKING thread-pool sequence and replies on the
  sequence that asked. Intuition is never touched from the UI thread.
- asl.library is opened around each requester rather than held for the
  process lifetime; a file dialog is rare.
- Multi-select results come back as WBArg entries, so each name is
  joined to its drawer through AddPart() - the only join that gets the
  AROS "Volume:dir/file" colon-vs-slash rule right.
- If asl.library will not open or the requester cannot be allocated, the
  listener is told the selection was cancelled. That path logs and
  continues; it never returns nullptr again.

Verified against the real pc-x86_64-smp SDK with x86_64-aros-g++: every
tag, FileRequester field and WBArg access compiles clean. Note STRPTR is
char* under C++ (exec/types.h swaps it deliberately) but wa_Name stays
BYTE*, so that one needs an explicit cast.

Not yet exercised on hardware - the requester's behaviour under a live
Chromium still needs a run.
